{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Review",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generates suggestions for improving readability, maintainability, and performance while maintaining existing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/*.zig",
      "tests/*.zig",
      "build.zig"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Review the recently modified code for potential improvements. Analyze for:\n\n1. **Code smells** — duplicated logic, overly long functions, deeply nested blocks, unclear naming\n2. **Design patterns** — opportunities to apply idiomatic Zig patterns, better use of comptime, improved error handling with error unions\n3. **Best practices** — proper use of allocators, defer for cleanup, slice vs pointer usage, avoiding unnecessary allocations\n4. **Readability** — naming clarity, function decomposition, comment quality\n5. **Performance** — unnecessary copies, allocation patterns, loop optimizations, cache-friendly access patterns\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions. Do not suggest changes that would alter existing functionality. Focus on the most impactful improvements rather than nitpicks."
  }
}